<body>
    <h1>AI-997: Milvus Vector Database Index Types</h1>
    <div class=3D"Section1">
        <h1 id=3D"AI-997:MilvusVectorDatabaseIndexTypes-MilvusVectorDatabas=
eIndexTypes:AComprehensiveTechnicalGuide">Milvus Vector Database Index Type=
s: A Comprehensive Technical Guide</h1>
<h2 id=3D"AI-997:MilvusVectorDatabaseIndexTypes-Summary">Summary</h2>
<p>In this document, I=E2=80=99ll try to provide a comprehensive analysis o=
f the various Milvus vector database index types, their technical implement=
ations, performance characteristics, and real-world applications. I will al=
so be making comparison of Milvus against Chroma (another vector databse). =
For this benchmarking I=E2=80=99m using<strong> 100k 768-dimensional vector=
s</strong> using <strong>ultra-dense clustering</strong> methodology.<br><b=
r>
I hope this guide serves as a definitive reference for selecting optimal ve=
ctor indexing strategies in our production environments around our AI drive=
n applications.</p>
<p><strong>TLDR:</strong></p>
<p><strong>Key Findings:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Milvus</strong> has a significantly higher recall than <strong>C=
hroma. </strong></p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>IVF_FLAT</strong> achieves perfect 100% recall but with higher c=
omputational cost</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>IVF_RABITQ</strong> delivers 92.4% recall with 23% better perfor=
mance than IVF_FLAT</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>HNSW</strong> provides excellent recall (98.4-100%) with balance=
d performance</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>IVF_PQ</strong> shows fundamental limitations with only 32.7% re=
call despite optimization.</p></li>
</ul>
<hr>
<h2 id=3D"AI-997:MilvusVectorDatabaseIndexTypes-Introduction">Introduction<=
/h2>
<p>Vector databases have become critical infrastructure for modern AI appli=
cations, powering everything from semantic search to recommendation systems=
. Milvus, as a leading open-source vector database, offers multiple indexin=
g strategies optimized for different use cases. In this guide, I=E2=80=99ll=
 try to provide the technical depth on each index type, backed by rigorous =
benchmarking data.</p>
<h3 id=3D"AI-997:MilvusVectorDatabaseIndexTypes-Firstly,WhyIndexSelectionMa=
tters?">Firstly, Why Index Selection Matters?</h3>
<p>The choice of vector index directly impacts:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Query Latency</strong>: Response times for similarity searches</=
p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Recall Accuracy</strong>: Percentage of relevant results returne=
d</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Memory Usage</strong>: RAM requirements for index storage</p></l=
i>
<li>
<p><strong>Build Time</strong>: Time required to construct the index</p></l=
i>
<li>
<p><strong>Throughput</strong>: Queries per second under load</p></li>
</ul>
<hr>
<h2 id=3D"AI-997:MilvusVectorDatabaseIndexTypes-Methodology&amp;Dataset">Me=
thodology &amp; Dataset</h2>
<h3 id=3D"AI-997:MilvusVectorDatabaseIndexTypes-BenchmarkConfiguration">Ben=
chmark Configuration</h3>
<p>During my benchmark, I used the following configuration:</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">Dataset=
 Specifications:
  - Size: 100,000 vectors
  - Dimensions: 768 (matching common embedding models)
  - Query Count: 10,000 queries (2,000 for detailed analysis)
  - Similarity Metric: Cosine similarity
  - Test Environment: Milvus v2.6 GPU standalone deployment</pre>
</div>
</div>
<h3 id=3D"AI-997:MilvusVectorDatabaseIndexTypes-DatasetGenerationStrategy">=
Dataset Generation Strategy</h3>
<p><strong>Ultra-Dense Clustering Approach:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>50 clusters</strong> with 2,000 vectors each</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Minimal noise injection</strong> (=CF=83 =3D 0.01) for tight clu=
ster cohesion</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>High-similarity queries</strong> (95% generated from cluster cen=
ters with =CF=83 =3D 0.005)</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Ground truth computation</strong> using brute-force cosine simil=
arity</p></li>
</ul>
<p>This methodology simulates real-world scenarios where:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Documents cluster around semantic topics</p></li>
<li>
<p>Users search for content similar to existing items</p></li>
<li>
<p>High recall is critical to the system or the end user.</p></li>
</ul>
<h3 id=3D"AI-997:MilvusVectorDatabaseIndexTypes-GroundTruthValidation">Grou=
nd Truth Validation</h3>
<p>Ground truth was computed using exact brute-force search with cosine sim=
ilarity, ensuring 100% accuracy for recall calculations across all k values=
 (1, 5, 10, 50, 100).</p>
<p>Before that, let=E2=80=99s understand what is recall all about.</p>
<h3 id=3D"AI-997:MilvusVectorDatabaseIndexTypes-WhatisRecall?">What is Reca=
ll?</h3>
<p><strong>Recall@k</strong> (also written as <strong>Recall@K</strong> or =
<strong>R@K</strong>) is a common evaluation metric, especially in informat=
ion retrieval tasks, recommendation systems and ML/AI driven tasks for sear=
ching and ranking.</p>
<p>It measures <strong>how many of the relevant (ground truth) items</stron=
g> are present in the <strong>top-K results</strong> returned by your syste=
m.</p>
<h4 id=3D"AI-997:MilvusVectorDatabaseIndexTypes-Example">Example</h4>
<p>Suppose there are <strong>5 relevant documents</strong> for a query.<br>
Your search engine returns a ranked list, and in the <strong>top 10</strong=
> results, <strong>4</strong> of those relevant documents appear.</p>
<p><strong>Recall@10=3D4/5 =3D 0.8 (80%)</strong></p>
<p>Now, let=E2=80=99s dive deep into the actual indexes.</p>
<hr>
<h2 id=3D"AI-997:MilvusVectorDatabaseIndexTypes-IndexTypesDeepDive">Index T=
ypes Deep Dive</h2>
<h3 id=3D"AI-997:MilvusVectorDatabaseIndexTypes-1.IVF_FLAT(InvertedFilewith=
FlatStorage)">1. IVF_FLAT (Inverted File with Flat Storage)</h3>
<h4 id=3D"AI-997:MilvusVectorDatabaseIndexTypes-TechnicalArchitecture">Tech=
nical Architecture</h4>
<p>IVF_FLAT uses an inverted file structure where:</p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p><strong>Clustering Phase</strong>: Vectors are partitioned into <code>nl=
ist</code> clusters using k-means</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Storage Phase</strong>: Each cluster stores vectors in their ori=
ginal precision</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Search Phase</strong>: Query searches <code>nprobe</code> neares=
t clusters exhaustively</p></li>
</ol>
<h4 id=3D"AI-997:MilvusVectorDatabaseIndexTypes-KeyParameters">Key Paramete=
rs</h4>
<div class=3D"table-wrap">
<table data-table-width=3D"760" data-layout=3D"default" data-local-id=3D"7a=
2feebf-9696-488d-9c60-092513938e7c" class=3D"confluenceTable">
<tbody>
<tr>
<th class=3D"confluenceTh">
<p>Parameter</p></th>
<th class=3D"confluenceTh">
<p>Description</p></th>
<th class=3D"confluenceTh">
<p>Impact</p></th>
<th class=3D"confluenceTh">
<p>Recommended Range</p></th>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><code>nlist</code></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Number of clusters</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Higher =3D better partitioning, longer build time</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>1024-4096</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><code>nprobe</code></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Clusters to search</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Higher =3D better recall, slower queries</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>10-50% of nlist</p></td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
<h4 id=3D"AI-997:MilvusVectorDatabaseIndexTypes-MathematicalFoundation">Mat=
hematical Foundation</h4>
<p>For a query vector <strong>q</strong>, IVF_FLAT:</p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>Computes distances to all cluster centroids: <code>d(q, c_i)</code></p><=
/li>
<li>
<p>Selects top <code>nprobe</code> clusters based on centroid distances</p>=
</li>
<li>
<p>Performs exhaustive search within selected clusters</p></li>
<li>
<p>Returns globally ranked results</p></li>
</ol>
<h4 id=3D"AI-997:MilvusVectorDatabaseIndexTypes-PerformanceCharacteristics"=
>Performance Characteristics</h4>
<p><strong>Strengths:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Perfect Recall</strong>: No approximation in distance computatio=
n</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Predictable Performance</strong>: Linear scaling with nprobe</p>=
</li>
<li>
<p><strong>No Compression Loss</strong>: Maintains full vector precision</p=
></li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Weaknesses:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>High Memory Usage</strong>: Stores full-precision vectors</p></l=
i>
<li>
<p><strong>Slower Queries</strong>: Exhaustive search within clusters</p></=
li>
<li>
<p><strong>Build Time</strong>: K-means clustering can be expensive</p></li=
>
</ul>
<h4 id=3D"AI-997:MilvusVectorDatabaseIndexTypes-BenchmarkResults">Benchmark=
 Results</h4>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">Configu=
ration: nlist=3D2048, nprobe=3D512
- Recall@1: 100.0%
- Recall@10: 100.0%
- Average Latency: 6.58ms
- Throughput: 152 QPS
- Memory: ~300MB for 100K vectors</pre>
</div>
</div>
<h3 id=3D"AI-997:MilvusVectorDatabaseIndexTypes-2.IVF_PQ(InvertedFilewithPr=
oductQuantization)">2. IVF_PQ (Inverted File with Product Quantization)</h3=
>
<h4 id=3D"AI-997:MilvusVectorDatabaseIndexTypes-TechnicalArchitecture.1">Te=
chnical Architecture</h4>
<p>IVF_PQ combines inverted file structure with product quantization compre=
ssion:</p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p><strong>Vector Partitioning</strong>: Split each vector into <code>m</co=
de> subvectors</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Codebook Learning</strong>: Train <code>m</code> codebooks with =
<code>2^nbits</code> centroids each</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Encoding</strong>: Replace subvectors with codebook indices</p><=
/li>
<li>
<p><strong>Search</strong>: Use asymmetric distance computation (ADC)</p></=
li>
</ol>
<h4 id=3D"AI-997:MilvusVectorDatabaseIndexTypes-KeyParameters.1">Key Parame=
ters</h4>
<div class=3D"table-wrap">
<table data-table-width=3D"760" data-layout=3D"default" data-local-id=3D"a3=
4a1345-a70d-4c6e-a442-a7f1b500e533" class=3D"confluenceTable">
<tbody>
<tr>
<th class=3D"confluenceTh">
<p>Parameter</p></th>
<th class=3D"confluenceTh">
<p>Description</p></th>
<th class=3D"confluenceTh">
<p>Impact</p></th>
<th class=3D"confluenceTh">
<p>Recommended Range</p></th>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><code>nlist</code></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Number of IVF clusters</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Partitioning quality</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>1024-4096</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><code>m</code></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Number of subvectors</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Compression vs accuracy</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>64-128</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><code>nbits</code></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Bits per subvector code</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Codebook size</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>8-16</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><code>nprobe</code></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Clusters to search</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Recall vs speed</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>10-50% of nlist</p></td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
<h4 id=3D"AI-997:MilvusVectorDatabaseIndexTypes-MathematicalFoundation.1">M=
athematical Foundation</h4>
<p><strong>Product Quantization Process:</strong></p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>Split vector <strong>x</strong> into subvectors: <code>x =3D [x=E2=82=81=
, x=E2=82=82, ..., x=E2=82=98]</code></p></li>
<li>
<p>Quantize each subvector: <code>q(x=E1=B5=A2) =3D arg min ||x=E1=B5=A2 - =
c=E1=B5=A2=E2=B1=BC||</code></p></li>
<li>
<p>Store indices: <code>code(x) =3D [j=E2=82=81, j=E2=82=82, ..., j=E2=82=
=98]</code></p></li>
</ol>
<p><strong>Distance Computation:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Symmetric</strong>: <code>d(q(x), q(y))</code> - both vectors qu=
antized</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Asymmetric</strong>: <code>d(x, q(y))</code> - query vector unqu=
antized (more accurate)</p></li>
</ul>
<h4 id=3D"AI-997:MilvusVectorDatabaseIndexTypes-PerformanceCharacteristics.=
1">Performance Characteristics</h4>
<p><strong>Strengths:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>High Compression</strong>: 16-64x size reduction typical</p></li=
>
<li>
<p><strong>Fast Search</strong>: Lookup-table based distance computation</p=
></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Memory Efficient</strong>: Suitable for large-scale deployments<=
/p></li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Weaknesses:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Significant Accuracy Loss</strong>: Quantization introduces appr=
oximation errors</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Parameter Sensitivity</strong>: Requires careful tuning of m and=
 nbits</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Training Overhead</strong>: Codebook learning phase</p></li>
</ul>
<h4 id=3D"AI-997:MilvusVectorDatabaseIndexTypes-BenchmarkResults.1">Benchma=
rk Results</h4>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">Configu=
ration: nlist=3D2048, m=3D128, nbits=3D16, nprobe=3D512
- Recall@1: 32.7% (=E2=9D=8C Poor performance)
- Recall@10: 46.1%
- Average Latency: 5.24ms
- Throughput: 191 QPS
- Memory: ~12MB for 100K vectors (25x compression)

Note: Despite aggressive optimization (m=3D128, nbits=3D16),=20
recall remained fundamentally limited by quantization artifacts.</pre>
</div>
</div>
<h3 id=3D"AI-997:MilvusVectorDatabaseIndexTypes-3.IVF_RABITQ(InvertedFilewi=
thResidualandBinaryQuantization)">3. IVF_RABITQ (Inverted File with Residua=
l and Binary Quantization)</h3>
<h4 id=3D"AI-997:MilvusVectorDatabaseIndexTypes-TechnicalArchitecture.2">Te=
chnical Architecture</h4>
<p>IVF_RABITQ represents Milvus's latest advanced quantization approach:</p=
>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p><strong>Residual Computation</strong>: Compute residuals after coarse qu=
antization</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Binary Quantization</strong>: Apply learned binary codes to resi=
duals</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Refinement Stage</strong>: Re-rank candidates using higher preci=
sion</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Adaptive Precision</strong>: Switch between quantized and refine=
d results</p></li>
</ol>
<h4 id=3D"AI-997:MilvusVectorDatabaseIndexTypes-KeyParameters.2">Key Parame=
ters</h4>
<div class=3D"table-wrap">
<table data-table-width=3D"760" data-layout=3D"default" data-local-id=3D"e6=
56ef03-e7ff-4b76-b6ed-f86955db82a1" class=3D"confluenceTable">
<tbody>
<tr>
<th class=3D"confluenceTh">
<p>Parameter</p></th>
<th class=3D"confluenceTh">
<p>Description</p></th>
<th class=3D"confluenceTh">
<p>Impact</p></th>
<th class=3D"confluenceTh">
<p>Recommended Range</p></th>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><code>nlist</code></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>IVF clusters</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Partitioning quality</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>1024-4096</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><code>refine</code></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Enable refinement</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Accuracy vs speed</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>true/false</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><code>refine_type</code></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Refinement precision</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>SQ8, FP16, FP32</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>FP16 recommended</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><code>refine_k</code></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Refinement multiplier</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Candidate pool size</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>2.0-4.0</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><code>rbq_query_bits</code></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Query quantization</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Speed vs accuracy</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>8</p></td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
<h4 id=3D"AI-997:MilvusVectorDatabaseIndexTypes-MathematicalFoundation.2">M=
athematical Foundation</h4>
<p><strong>Residual-Based Quantization:</strong></p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>Coarse quantization: <code>r =3D x - q_coarse(x)</code></p></li>
<li>
<p>Binary quantization of residual: <code>b =3D sign(r - =CE=BC)</code></p>=
</li>
<li>
<p>Distance approximation: <code>d(x,y) =E2=89=88 d_coarse + d_binary(r_x, =
r_y)</code></p></li>
</ol>
<p><strong>Refinement Process:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Select top <code>k =C3=97 refine_k</code> candidates using quantized dis=
tances</p></li>
<li>
<p>Re-compute exact distances for refinement pool</p></li>
<li>
<p>Return top-k from refined results</p></li>
</ul>
<h4 id=3D"AI-997:MilvusVectorDatabaseIndexTypes-PerformanceCharacteristics.=
2">Performance Characteristics</h4>
<p><strong>Strengths:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Excellent Recall</strong>: 92-93% with proper tuning</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Balanced Performance</strong>: Good speed-accuracy tradeoff</p><=
/li>
<li>
<p><strong>Adaptive Precision</strong>: Refinement improves accuracy when n=
eeded</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Memory Efficient</strong>: Significant compression with quality =
retention</p></li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Weaknesses:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Complex Tuning</strong>: Multiple interdependent parameters</p><=
/li>
<li>
<p><strong>Refinement Overhead</strong>: Additional computation for high ac=
curacy</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Implementation Complexity</strong>: More sophisticated than the =
basic indexes</p></li>
</ul>
<h4 id=3D"AI-997:MilvusVectorDatabaseIndexTypes-BenchmarkResults.2">Benchma=
rk Results</h4>
