<h2 id=3D"AI-997:MilvusVectorDatabaseIndexTypes-MilvusvsChromaComparison">M=
ilvus vs Chroma Comparison</h2>
<h3 id=3D"AI-997:MilvusVectorDatabaseIndexTypes-BenchmarkMethodology">Bench=
mark Methodology</h3>
<h4 id=3D"AI-997:MilvusVectorDatabaseIndexTypes-DatasetGeneration">Dataset =
Generation</h4>
<p>The benchmark used a carefully designed dataset to ensure fair and meani=
ngful comparison:</p>
<p><strong>Dataset Specifications:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Size</strong>: 100,000 vectors</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Dimensions</strong>: 768 (matching common embedding models like =
sentence-transformers)</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Distribution</strong>: Ultra-dense clustering approach</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Clusters</strong>: 50 clusters with 2,000 vectors each</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Noise Level</strong>: =CF=83 =3D 0.01 for tight cluster cohesion=
</p></li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Dataset Generation Process:</strong></p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: py; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence"># Generat=
e cluster centers
for cluster_id in range(50):
    cluster_center =3D np.random.randn(768).astype(np.float32)
    cluster_center =3D cluster_center / np.linalg.norm(cluster_center)  # N=
ormalize
   =20
    # Generate vectors around each center
    for i in range(2000):
        noise =3D np.random.randn(768).astype(np.float32) * 0.01=20
        vector =3D cluster_center + noise
        vector =3D vector / np.linalg.norm(vector)  # Normalize
       =20
        # Store with unique ID
        vector_id =3D f"vec_{cluster_id:04d}_{i:06d}"
        raw_vectors.append(vector.tolist())
        raw_ids.append(vector_id)</pre>
</div>
</div>
<h4 id=3D"AI-997:MilvusVectorDatabaseIndexTypes-QueryGeneration">Query Gene=
ration</h4>
<p><strong>Query Strategy:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Total Queries</strong>: 10,000 generated, 2,000 used for detaile=
d analysis</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>High-Similarity Queries</strong>: 95% generated from existing cl=
uster centers</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Query Noise</strong>: =CF=83 =3D 0.005 for maximum similarity to=
 dataset</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Random Queries</strong>: 5% completely random for diversity</p><=
/li>
</ul>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: py; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence"># Query g=
eneration process
for i in range(query_count):
    if np.random.random() &lt; 0.95:  # 95% high-similarity
        cluster_idx =3D i % len(cluster_centers)
        base_vector =3D cluster_centers[cluster_idx]
        noise =3D np.random.randn(768).astype(np.float32) * 0.005
        query =3D base_vector + noise
    else:  # 5% random
        query =3D np.random.randn(768).astype(np.float32)
   =20
    query =3D query / np.linalg.norm(query) # Normalize
    query_vectors.append(query.tolist())</pre>
</div>
</div>
<h4 id=3D"AI-997:MilvusVectorDatabaseIndexTypes-GroundTruthComputation">Gro=
und Truth Computation</h4>
<p><strong>Brute-Force Baseline:</strong><br>
Ground truth was computed using exact cosine similarity calculation:</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: py; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence"># Ground =
truth computation
db_vectors =3D np.array(raw_vectors, dtype=3Dnp.float32)  # 100K x 768
ground_truth =3D {}

for k in [1, 5, 10, 50, 100]:
    ground_truth[k] =3D []
   =20
    for query_vec in query_sample:  # 2K queries
        # Compute actual cosine similarities
        similarities =3D np.dot(db_vectors, np.array(query_vec, dtype=3Dnp.=
float32))
       =20
        # Get top-k vectors
        top_k_indices =3D np.argsort(similarities)[::-1][:k]
        top_k_ids =3D [raw_ids[idx] for idx in top_k_indices]
       =20
        ground_truth[k].append(top_k_ids)</pre>
</div>
</div>
<h4 id=3D"AI-997:MilvusVectorDatabaseIndexTypes-RecallCalculationMethodolog=
y">Recall Calculation Methodology</h4>
<p><strong>ID-Based Comparison:</strong><br>
Recall calculation will be purely based on vector ID matching, independent =
of distance/similarity values, since Milvus uses Cosine similarity (higher=
=3Dbetter), while Chroma uses Cosine distance(lower=3Dbetter).</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: py; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence"># Recall =
calculation for both Milvus and Chroma
for k in k_values:
    recall_sum =3D 0.0
    for i, search_result in enumerate(search_results):
        if i &lt; len(ground_truth[k]):
            search_top_k =3D set(search_result[:k])  # IDs from search
            gt_top_k =3D set(ground_truth[k][i])     # IDs from ground trut=
h
           =20
            # Calculate recall
            intersection =3D len(search_top_k.intersection(gt_top_k))
            recall =3D intersection / len(gt_top_k)
            recall_sum +=3D recall
   =20
    recalls[f"recall@{k}"] =3D recall_sum / len(search_results)</pre>
</div>
</div>
<p><strong>Key Points:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Both systems return vector IDs from their search results</p></li>
<li>
<p>Ground truth contains the correct IDs for each query</p></li>
<li>
<p>Recall =3D (# correct IDs returned) / (# total correct IDs)</p></li>
<li>
<p>Distance/similarity values are not used in recall calculation</p></li>
</ul>
<h3 id=3D"AI-997:MilvusVectorDatabaseIndexTypes-SystemConfiguration">System=
 Configuration</h3>
<h4 id=3D"AI-997:MilvusVectorDatabaseIndexTypes-MilvusSetup">Milvus Setup</=
h4>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: py; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence"># Collect=
ion creation
schema =3D MilvusClient.create_schema(auto_id=3DFalse, enable_dynamic_field=
=3DTrue)
schema.add_field(field_name=3D"id", datatype=3DDataType.VARCHAR, max_length=
=3D50, is_primary=3DTrue)
schema.add_field(field_name=3D"embedding", datatype=3DDataType.FLOAT_VECTOR=
, dim=3D768)
schema.add_field(field_name=3D"metadata", datatype=3DDataType.JSON)

# Index creation with cosine metric
index_params_obj.add_index(
    field_name=3D"embedding",
    index_type=3Dindex_type,  # IVF_FLAT, IVF_RABITQ, HNSW, etc.
    metric_type=3D"COSINE",
    params=3Dindex_params # Index specific params
)</pre>
</div>
</div>
<h4 id=3D"AI-997:MilvusVectorDatabaseIndexTypes-ChromaSetup">Chroma Setup</=
h4>
