<h3 id=3D"AI-997:MilvusVectorDatabaseIndexTypes-KeyFindings">Key Findings</=
h3>
<h4 id=3D"AI-997:MilvusVectorDatabaseIndexTypes-PerformanceGapAnalysis">Per=
formance Gap Analysis</h4>
<p><strong>Recall Performance:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Milvus HNSW</strong>: Consistently achieves 98.5-99.7% recall ac=
ross configurations</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Chroma HNSW</strong>: Achieves 60.3-82.8% recall with identical =
parameters</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Gap</strong>: Milvus shows 17-39 percentage point advantage in r=
ecall</p></li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Latency Performance:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Milvus</strong>: 4.93-7.62ms average latency</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Chroma</strong>: 4.28-7.27ms average latency</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Gap</strong>: Similar latency performance, slight Chroma advanta=
ge</p></li>
</ul>
<h4 id=3D"AI-997:MilvusVectorDatabaseIndexTypes-TechnicalDifferences">Techn=
ical Differences</h4>
<p><strong>Implementation Variations:</strong></p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p><strong>HNSW Library</strong>: Milvus uses optimized internal implementa=
tion vs Chroma's hnswlib</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Parameter Interpretation</strong>: Same parameter values may beh=
ave differently</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Index Building</strong>: Different optimization strategies durin=
g construction</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Search Algorithm</strong>: Subtle differences in graph traversal=
 and candidate selection</p></li>
</ol>
<p><strong>Milvus Advantages:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Index Variety</strong>: IVF_FLAT, IVF_PQ, IVF_RABITQ, multiple H=
NSW variants</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Advanced Quantization</strong>: RABITQ achieves 92.5% recall wit=
h significant compression</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Optimization Maturity</strong>: Highly tuned implementations acr=
oss all index types</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Enterprise Features</strong>: Distributed architecture, RBAC, ba=
ckup/restore</p></li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Chroma Advantages:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Simplicity</strong>: Easier setup and integration for basic use =
cases</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Python Native</strong>: Seamless ML workflow integration</p></li=
>
<li>
<p><strong>Lightweight</strong>: Lower resource overhead for small datasets=
</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Document Model</strong>: Natural fit for document-based applicat=
ions</p></li>
</ul>
<hr>
