<h2 id=3D"AI-997:MilvusVectorDatabaseIndexTypes-PerformanceComparison">Perf=
ormance Comparison</h2>
<h3 id=3D"AI-997:MilvusVectorDatabaseIndexTypes-SpeedvsAccuracyTradeoff">Sp=
eed vs Accuracy Tradeoff</h3>
<p>The benchmark reveals clear performance tiers:</p>
<h4 id=3D"AI-997:MilvusVectorDatabaseIndexTypes-Tier1:HighAccuracy(>95%Reca=
ll)">Tier 1: High Accuracy (&gt;95% Recall)</h4>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>IVF_FLAT</strong>: Perfect accuracy, moderate speed</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>HNSW (High-end)</strong>: Near-Perfect accuracy, good speed</p><=
/li>
<li>
<p><strong>HNSW_SQ</strong>: Excellent accuracy, best speed in tier with co=
mpression and FP16 refinement</p></li>
</ul>
<h4 id=3D"AI-997:MilvusVectorDatabaseIndexTypes-Tier2:BalancedPerformance(9=
0-95%Recall)">Tier 2: Balanced Performance (90-95% Recall)</h4>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>IVF_RABITQ</strong>: Excellent balance of accuracy and speed</p>=
</li>
<li>
<p><strong>HNSW (Standard)</strong>: Very good accuracy, consistent perform=
ance</p></li>
</ul>
<h4 id=3D"AI-997:MilvusVectorDatabaseIndexTypes-Tier3:Speed-Optimized(80-90=
%Recall)">Tier 3: Speed-Optimized (80-90% Recall)</h4>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>HNSW_PQ/PRQ</strong>: Good accuracy with compression benefits</p=
></li>
</ul>
<h4 id=3D"AI-997:MilvusVectorDatabaseIndexTypes-Tier4:HighCompression(<50%R=
ecall)">Tier 4: High Compression (&lt;50% Recall)</h4>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>IVF_PQ</strong>: Extreme compression but poor accuracy</p></li>
</ul>
<h3 id=3D"AI-997:MilvusVectorDatabaseIndexTypes-KeyPerformanceInsights">Key=
 Performance Insights</h3>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p><strong>IVF_RABITQ Emergence</strong>: Delivers 92.4% recall with compet=
itive performance, representing the best balance for production use.</p></l=
i>
<li>
<p><strong>HNSW Consistency</strong>: Provides predictable high performance=
 across configurations, making it reliable for critical applications.</p></=
li>
<li>
<p><strong>IVF_PQ Limitations</strong>: Despite optimization efforts, funda=
mental quantization losses limit its applicability to scenarios where high =
recall is not critical.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Memory-Performance Tradeoff</strong>: Clear correlation between =
compression ratio and accuracy loss, with RABITQ offering the best compromi=
se.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Milvus vs Chroma</strong>: Milvus demonstrates significant recal=
l advantage (98.5-99.7% vs 60.3-82.8%) and superior index variety, while Ch=
roma offers simplicity for basic use cases.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Quantization Advantage</strong>: Milvus's advanced quantization =
(RABITQ, SQ) provides significant memory savings while maintaining high rec=
all, unavailable in Chroma.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Implementation Quality</strong>: The substantial recall gap sugg=
ests Milvus's HNSW implementation is more mature and optimized than Chroma'=
s hnswlib-based approach.</p></li>
</ol>
<hr>
<h2 id=3D"AI-997:MilvusVectorDatabaseIndexTypes-Real-WorldUseCases">Real-Wo=
rld Use Cases</h2>
<p>Here are some sample real world use cases demonstrating the type of inde=
x to be used based on the requirement. <br><em>Note: These are just some th=
eoretical values based on the real world need and the performance benchmark=
s.</em></p>
<h3 id=3D"AI-997:MilvusVectorDatabaseIndexTypes-E-commerceProductSearch"><b=
r>
E-commerce Product Search</h3>
<p><strong>Scenario</strong>: Fashion retailer with 10M product images<br><=
strong>Requirements</strong>: &lt;100ms response time, &gt;95% recall for v=
isual similarity</p>
<p><strong>Recommended Solution</strong>: HNSW_SQ</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">Configu=
ration:
  index_type: HNSW_SQ
  M: 64
  efConstruction: 800
  sq_type: SQ8
  refine: true
  refine_type: FP16
  ef: 1200
  refine_k: 2.0

Expected Performance:
  - Recall@10: 99.1%
  - Latency: ~6ms
  - Memory: 4x compression
  - Throughput: 161 QPS</pre>
</div>
</div>
<p><strong>Rationale</strong>: Excellent recall with memory efficiency, sui=
table for large product catalogs.</p>
<h3 id=3D"AI-997:MilvusVectorDatabaseIndexTypes-DocumentSemanticSearch">Doc=
ument Semantic Search</h3>
<p><strong>Scenario</strong>: Enterprise knowledge base with 1M documents<b=
r><strong>Requirements</strong>: Perfect recall for critical information re=
trieval</p>
<p><strong>Recommended Solution</strong>: IVF_FLAT</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">Configu=
ration:
  index_type: IVF_FLAT
  nlist: 2048
  nprobe: 512

Expected Performance:
  - Recall@10: 100%
  - Latency: ~7ms
  - Memory: Full precision
  - Throughput: 152 QPS</pre>
</div>
</div>
<p><strong>Rationale</strong>: Perfect recall ensures no critical documents=
 are missed.</p>
<h3 id=3D"AI-997:MilvusVectorDatabaseIndexTypes-Real-timeRecommendationSyst=
em">Real-time Recommendation System</h3>
<p><strong>Scenario</strong>: Social media platform with 100M user profiles=
<br><strong>Requirements</strong>: &lt;5ms response time, acceptable accura=
cy loss</p>
<p><strong>Recommended Solution</strong>: IVF_RABITQ with FP16</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">Configu=
ration:
  index_type: IVF_RABITQ
  nlist: 4096
  refine: true
  refine_type: FP16
  nprobe: 256
  refine_k: 2.0

Expected Performance:
  - Recall@10: 79.3%
  - Latency: ~5ms
  - Memory: 7x compression
  - Throughput: 192 QPS</pre>
</div>
</div>
<p><strong>Rationale</strong>: Optimized for speed while maintaining reason=
able accuracy for recommendations.</p>
<h3 id=3D"AI-997:MilvusVectorDatabaseIndexTypes-ContentModeration">Content =
Moderation</h3>
<p><strong>Scenario</strong>: Video platform scanning for inappropriate con=
tent<br><strong>Requirements</strong>: High throughput, memory efficiency, =
good accuracy</p>
<p><strong>Recommended Solution</strong>: HNSW_PQ</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">Configu=
ration:
  index_type: HNSW_PQ
  M: 64
  efConstruction: 800
  m: 96
  nbits: 8
  refine: true
  refine_type: FP16
  ef: 1200
  refine_k: 2.0

Expected Performance:
  - Recall@10: 76.7%
  - Latency: ~9ms
  - Memory: 9x compression
  - Throughput: 115 QPS</pre>
</div>
</div>
<p><strong>Rationale</strong>: Good compression for large-scale deployment =
with acceptable accuracy for content filtering.</p>
<h3 id=3D"AI-997:MilvusVectorDatabaseIndexTypes-FinancialFraudDetection">Fi=
nancial Fraud Detection</h3>
<p><strong>Scenario</strong>: Transaction pattern analysis for fraud detect=
ion<br><strong>Requirements</strong>: Perfect recall (cannot miss fraud), r=
eal-time processing</p>
<p><strong>Recommended Solution</strong>: HNSW (High Quality)</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">Configu=
ration:
  index_type: HNSW
  M: 96
  efConstruction: 1200
  ef: 2400

Expected Performance:
  - Recall@10: 100%
  - Latency: ~10ms
  - Memory: Standard
  - Throughput: 96 QPS</pre>
</div>
</div>
<p><strong>Rationale</strong>: Perfect recall is critical for fraud detecti=
on; slightly higher latency is acceptable.</p>
