<h3 id=3D"AI-997:MilvusVectorDatabaseIndexTypes-ParameterTuningGuidelines">=
Parameter Tuning Guidelines</h3>
<h4 id=3D"AI-997:MilvusVectorDatabaseIndexTypes-IVF-basedIndexes">IVF-based=
 Indexes</h4>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence"># Conse=
rvative (High Recall)
nlist: dataset_size / 50  # Denser clusters
nprobe: nlist * 0.25      # 25% cluster coverage

# Aggressive (High Speed)
nlist: dataset_size / 100 # Larger clusters
nprobe: nlist * 0.10      # 10% cluster coverage</pre>
</div>
</div>
<h4 id=3D"AI-997:MilvusVectorDatabaseIndexTypes-HNSW-basedIndexes">HNSW-bas=
ed Indexes</h4>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence"># High =
Quality
M: 64-96
efConstruction: 800-1200
ef: 1200-2400

# Balanced
M: 32-64
efConstruction: 400-800
ef: 400-1200

# Speed Optimized
M: 16-32
efConstruction: 200-400
ef: 100-400</pre>
</div>
</div>
<h4 id=3D"AI-997:MilvusVectorDatabaseIndexTypes-RABITQRefinement">RABITQ Re=
finement</h4>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence"># High =
Accuracy
refine_k: 3.0-4.0
refine_type: FP16

# Balanced
refine_k: 2.0-3.0
refine_type: SQ8

# Speed Optimized
refine_k: 1.0-2.0
refine_type: SQ8</pre>
</div>
</div>
<hr>
<h2 id=3D"AI-997:MilvusVectorDatabaseIndexTypes-TechnicalImplementationGuid=
elines">Technical Implementation Guidelines</h2>
<h4 id=3D"AI-997:MilvusVectorDatabaseIndexTypes-InfrastructureRequirements"=
>Infrastructure Requirements</h4>
<p><em>Note: I will write a more detailed and comprehensive guide with rega=
rds to the infra requirements and memory planning later on, but here are my=
 initial thoughts.</em></p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p><strong>Memory Planning</strong></p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence"># Calcu=
late memory requirements
IVF_FLAT: vectors * dimensions * 4 bytes * 1.2 (overhead)
HNSW: vectors * dimensions * 4 bytes * 1.5 (graph overhead)
IVF_RABITQ: vectors * dimensions * 4 bytes * 0.15 (compression)</pre>
</div>
</div></li>
<li>
<p><strong>CPU Considerations</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>IVF indexes: CPU-intensive during nprobe search</p></li>
<li>
<p>HNSW indexes: Memory bandwidth sensitive</p></li>
<li>
<p>Quantized indexes: Lower CPU usage but more complex</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Storage Requirements</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Index persistence: Plan for 2x memory for safe rebuilds</p></li>
<li>
<p>Backup strategy: Consider index rebuild time vs storage cost</p></li>
</ul></li>
</ol>
<h4 id=3D"AI-997:MilvusVectorDatabaseIndexTypes-ConfigurationOptimization:"=
>Configuration Optimization:</h4>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p><strong>Index Building</strong></p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: py; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence"># Optimiz=
ed index creation
index_params =3D {
    "index_type": "IVF_RABITQ",
    "params": {
        "nlist": min(4096, dataset_size // 50),
        "refine": True,
        "refine_type": "SQ8"
    }
}

# Build with adequate resources
collection.create_index(
    field_name=3D"embedding",
    index_params=3Dindex_params,
    timeout=3D3600  # Allow sufficient time
)</pre>
</div>
</div></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Search Optimization</strong></p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: py; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence"># Adaptiv=
e search parameters
search_params =3D {
    "nprobe": max(16, nlist // 8),
    "refine_k": 3.0,
    "rbq_query_bits": 8
}

# Batch queries for efficiency
results =3D collection.search(
    data=3Dquery_batch,
    anns_field=3D"embedding",
    param=3Dsearch_params,
    limit=3Dtopk,
    batch_size=3D100
)</pre>
</div>
</div></li>
</ol>
<hr>
<h2 id=3D"AI-997:MilvusVectorDatabaseIndexTypes-Conclusions&amp;Recommendat=
ions">Conclusions &amp; Recommendations</h2>
<h3 id=3D"AI-997:MilvusVectorDatabaseIndexTypes-KeyFindingsSummary">Key Fin=
dings Summary</h3>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p><strong>IVF_RABITQ Emerges as a balance of accuracy and speed</strong>: =
With 92.4% recall and competitive performance, IVF_RABITQ represents the op=
timal balance for most production scenarios.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>HNSW Provides Reliability</strong>: Consistent high performance =
across configurations makes HNSW ideal for critical applications requiring =
predictable behavior.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>IVF_PQ Has Limited Applicability</strong>: Despite extensive opt=
imization, fundamental quantization limitations restrict IVF_PQ to scenario=
s where extreme compression outweighs accuracy requirements.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Parameter Tuning is Critical</strong>: Proper configuration can =
improve recall by 20-30% while maintaining performance targets.</p></li>
</ol>
<h3 id=3D"AI-997:MilvusVectorDatabaseIndexTypes-FutureConsiderations">Futur=
e Considerations</h3>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p><strong>Hardware Evolution</strong>: GPU acceleration may change perform=
ance characteristics</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Algorithm Advances</strong>: New quantization techniques may imp=
rove compression-accuracy tradeoffs</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Workload Evolution</strong>: Monitor data distribution changes t=
hat may require index re-selection</p></li>
</ol>
